    "narrative": "Our strongest play today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.52), who benefits from a favorable matchup against Rocker and a critical situational edge; his ability to capitalize on a slow SP delivery provides a tangible boost to our stolen base efficiency. **Tyler Freeman** (70.02) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.94) round out our top-tier starts. **Tyler Freeman** is bolstered by an elite park factor and a favorable spot in the two-hole, while **Daulton Varsho** is perfectly positioned to exploit a weak outing from Young, supported by a significant 18% SP skill advantage and strong platoon splits. Additionally, the quartet of **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Drew Gilbert** will enjoy wind-aided conditions against Cabrera, E, with the former three providing high-floor production that makes them essential starters in today\u2019s format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Jonathan Aranda** (47.25) out of the UTIL spot. While he boasts a strong xwOBA, his score was suppressed by a tough matchup against Gusto (2.88 xERA), ultimately giving the nod to **Matt Chapman** (59.72) due to the higher projected efficiency and favorable stadium variables. We are monitoring **Will Smith** (40.79) closely today; while he is in the lineup, his low score is a direct result of Detmers\u2019 ability to suppress production, keeping him dangerously close to our benching threshold. With **Cal Raleigh** still on the IL and **Lawrence Butler** not in the starting rotation, we are relying on our depth players to maintain our standing in the stolen base category, where we continue to leverage the speed profiles of **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo** despite middling matchup projections.",
